window.products.push({"id":146114,"name":"WR60X10220 Refrigerator Condenser Fan Motor AP4298602 WR60X10171 WR60X10133 PS1766247 AH1766247 EA1766247 WR60X10192 1257132 Hotpoint GE Ultra Durable","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":11.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/614ucwCDxKL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Ge Wr60x10220 Condenser Fan Motor - A high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers AP4298602, 1257132, AH1766247, EA1766247, PS1766247, WR60X10133, WR60X10171, WR60X10192. Condenser Fan Motor Wr60x10220 is compatible with General Electric, Hotpoint appliances. It is responsible for circulating air over the condenser coils, which helps to dissipate heat and keep the refrigerator cool. Wr60x10220 Ge Generator Fan Motor fits hundreds of models and can be installed in a few minutes. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the Wr60x10220 Condenser Fan Motor? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Wr60x10220 Fan Motor will help if your appliance is noisy, freezer or fridge section is too warm, or it does not start. Replacing the condenser fan motor is a fairly simple process that can be completed by most DIYers with basic tools and some mechanical aptitude. 💡 The condenser fan motor is located at the back of the refrigerator. It is typically a small, cylindrical motor with a shaft that extends through the back of the refrigerator and connects to a fan blade. When the motor is activated, the fan blade spins rapidly, drawing air over the condenser coils and expelling it out the back of the refrigerator. Wr60x10220 Condenser Fan Motor meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 The Ge Wr60x10220 Motor Condenser Fan For Refrigerator operates on 115 volts AC and has a power rating of 9 watts. It is designed to operate at a maximum speed of 1550 RPM, and has a single-speed operation. The Ge Condenser Fan Motor Wr60x10220 is capable of producing a maximum airflow of 80 cubic feet per minute (CFM), which is sufficient to keep the condenser coils cool and maintain the proper temperature inside the refrigerator. 💡 How to test refrigerator condenser fan motor with multimeter? To do so, first turn off the power to the refrigerator, then locate and disconnect the wires from the fan motor. Set the multimeter to measure resistance and touch the multimeter leads to the terminals on the fan motor. Check the reading on the multimeter, and a good condenser fan motor should have a resistance reading between 20 and 200 ohms. Reconnect the wires to the fan motor and turn the power back on to the refrigerator.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/614ucwCDxKL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B07KPKY2HH","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-146114","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07KPKY2HH","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B07KPKY2HH","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
